# ClauseFlag Development Instructions for OpenCode CLI

## Project Overview
ClauseFlag is a MicroSaaS contract clause risk scanner. It identifies high-risk clauses in contracts within 60 seconds for SMBs, founders, and freelancers. This is an MVP focused on speed, simplicity, and actionable insights—NOT comprehensive legal analysis.

## Core Technical Stack
- Frontend: Next.js 14+ (App Router), React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Backend: Next.js API Routes, Node.js
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- AI: OpenAI GPT-4 or Claude (structured JSON output)
- Document Parsing: pdfplumber (PDF), python-docx (DOCX)
- Payments: Stripe
- Hosting: Vercel
- Auth: Supabase Auth (Phase 2)

## Mandatory Coding Principles

### RELIABILITY
- Use TypeScript strict mode, no `any` types
- Wrap all async operations in try-catch with specific error messages
- Validate all inputs (file type, size, format) client AND server-side
- Implement comprehensive error boundaries in React components
- Use Zod schemas for API request/response validation
- Never crash user experience—always provide fallback UI
- Log errors with context (Winston/Pino) but never log sensitive data
- Implement retry logic with exponential backoff for AI API calls
- Sanitize all file uploads, validate MIME types server-side

### PERFORMANCE
- Target: < 60 seconds total processing, < 3 seconds API response
- Use React Server Components by default, client components only when needed
- Implement Suspense boundaries for async operations
- Lazy load heavy dependencies: `const parser = await import('pdfplumber')`
- Stream AI responses to improve perceived performance
- Cache parsed documents and clause analyses (Redis or in-memory for MVP)
- Process multiple clauses in parallel with `Promise.all()` and concurrency limits
- Use Next.js Image component, optimize assets
- Keep client bundle < 200KB gzipped
- Index database frequently: user_email, contract_id, created_at, status

### CODE HEALTH
- Single Responsibility Principle: one function = one purpose
- DRY: create reusable utilities for parsing, AI prompts, risk scoring
- Clear naming: `extractClausesFromPDF()` not `processDoc()`
- JSDoc comments for all exported functions
- Folder structure by domain:
